 "fraud_controls_note": "\u2022 Fraud controls and their timing. Basic duplicate-applicant checks have been part of decisioning since May 2026 and the first set of major improvements to our second generation credit model were released on 5 May 2026 (v2.1). Version 2.1 sharply reduced uncoordinated first-payment default on new accounts: first-payment defaults fell from 1.2\u20131.5% of cards issued in February\u2013April 2026 to 0.4% of cards issued in May\u2013August. On 24 October 2026 Zed deployed a full suite of fraud-signal policies, informed by its review of first-payment defaults: bank account numbers shared across applicants, repeated selfie or ID images, invite-name mismatches, business-owner income verification and past-due bureau tradelines.",
